<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves slip to $1.95 bln.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves slip to $1.95 bln.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's central bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.958 billion on Feb 7, down $38 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In January 1997, international reserves grew $164 million.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of last year, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
